    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Refine OpenMP directives to optimize work sharing, reductions, scheduling, and thread granularity for the sliding window technique in finding the maximum sum submatrix.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Add #include <omp.h> at the beginning of the file.\",\n    \"Use parallel for directive with reduction clause for the initial sum calculation.\",\n    \"Use parallel for directive with collapse clause to optimize nested loops in the sliding window technique.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n,s;\\n\\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\\n\\tstd::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n\\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n\\tassert(s<n);\\n\\tassert(n<8000);\\n\\tassert(s>0);\\n\\tassert(n>0);\\n\\n\\tint sum = 0;\\n\\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum) collapse(2)\\n\\tfor(int i=0;i<s;i++)\\n\\t\\tfor(int j=0;j<s;j++)\\n\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\n\\tint mxSum = sum;\\n\\n\\tint dir = 1;\\n\\tint i = 0;\\n\\tint j = 0;\\n\\twhile(i+s <= n) {\\n\\t\\tif( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) { \\n\\t\\t\\tint exitingRow = i;\\n\\t\\t\\tint enteringRow = exitingRow+s;\\n\\t\\t\\tif(enteringRow >=n) break;\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(-:sum)\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum -= matrix[exitingRow][k+j]; } \\n\\t\\t\\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) { sum += matrix[enteringRow][k+j];\\t} \\n\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\ti++;\\n\\t\\t\\tdir*=-1;\\n\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\tint exitingCol,enteringCol;\\n\\t\\t\\tif(dir==1) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\texitingCol = j;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tenteringCol = exitingCol + s;\\n\\t\\t\\t} else {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tenteringCol = j-1;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\texitingCol = enteringCol + s;\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(-:sum)\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum -= matrix[k+i][exitingCol]; } \\n\\t\\t\\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)\\n\\t\\t\\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {sum += matrix[k+i][enteringCol];\\t} \\n\\t\\t\\tj+=dir;\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\\n\\t}\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\",mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Added OpenMP directives to parallelize the initial sum calculation and the sliding window technique. Used reduction clauses for sum operations to ensure correct accumulation of results across threads.\"\n}"
